2026-09-05 09:40:00  Setup: built watchdog.sh (auto-resume). Watches logs/progress.log; if it goes quiet for 15 min it parses the usage-limit reset time out of the newest ~/.claude/projects transcript, sleeps until reset + 3 min buffer, then runs `claude --continue --dangerously-skip-permissions`. Start with: nohup bash watchdog.sh > logs/watchdog.log 2>&1 &  / stop with: bash watchdog.sh --stop
2026-09-05 09:40:00  CAVEAT logged in watchdog.sh header: `claude --continue` reattaches to the most recent CLI session for this folder. If the build is driven from the Claude desktop app rather than a terminal, it cannot resume that exact session. For reliable overnight auto-resume, run the build from a terminal (`claude --dangerously-skip-permissions`) with the watchdog alongside.
